{"path":".agents/skills/domain-modeling/SKILL.md","ref":"1f305ea273a1133774b6a1eda851a5ad99278ad3","side":"old","lines":[{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":1,"text":"---"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":2,"text":"name: domain-modeling"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":3,"text":"description: Build and sharpen a project's domain model. Use when the user wants to pin down domain terminology or a ubiquitous language, record an architectural decision, or when another skill needs to maintain the domain model."},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":4,"text":"---"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":5,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":6,"text":"# Domain Modeling"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":7,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":8,"text":"Actively build and sharpen the project's domain model as you design. This is the *active* discipline — challenging terms, inventing edge-case scenarios, and writing the glossary and decisions down the moment they crystallise. (Merely *reading* `CONTEXT.md` for vocabulary is not this skill — that's a one-line habit any skill can do. This skill is for when you're changing the model, not just consuming it.)"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":9,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":10,"text":"## File structure"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":11,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":12,"text":"Most repos have a single context:"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":13,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":14,"text":"```"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":15,"text":"/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":16,"text":"├── CONTEXT.md"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":17,"text":"├── docs/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":18,"text":"│   └── adr/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":19,"text":"│       ├── 0001-event-sourced-orders.md"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":20,"text":"│       └── 0002-postgres-for-write-model.md"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":21,"text":"└── src/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":22,"text":"```"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":23,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":24,"text":"If a `CONTEXT-MAP.md` exists at the root, the repo has multiple contexts. The map points to where each one lives:"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":25,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":26,"text":"```"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":27,"text":"/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":28,"text":"├── CONTEXT-MAP.md"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":29,"text":"├── docs/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":30,"text":"│   └── adr/                          ← system-wide decisions"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":31,"text":"├── src/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":32,"text":"│   ├── ordering/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":33,"text":"│   │   ├── CONTEXT.md"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":34,"text":"│   │   └── docs/adr/                 ← context-specific decisions"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":35,"text":"│   └── billing/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":36,"text":"│       ├── CONTEXT.md"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":37,"text":"│       └── docs/adr/"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":38,"text":"```"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":39,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":40,"text":"Create files lazily — only when you have something to write. If no `CONTEXT.md` exists, create one when the first term is resolved. If no `docs/adr/` exists, create it when the first ADR is needed."},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":41,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":42,"text":"## During the session"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":43,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":44,"text":"### Challenge against the glossary"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":45,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":46,"text":"When the user uses a term that conflicts with the existing language in `CONTEXT.md`, call it out immediately. \"Your glossary defines 'cancellation' as X, but you seem to mean Y — which is it?\""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":47,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":48,"text":"### Sharpen fuzzy language"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":49,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":50,"text":"When the user uses vague or overloaded terms, propose a precise canonical term. \"You're saying 'account' — do you mean the Customer or the User? Those are different things.\""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":51,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":52,"text":"### Discuss concrete scenarios"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":53,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":54,"text":"When domain relationships are being discussed, stress-test them with specific scenarios. Invent scenarios that probe edge cases and force the user to be precise about the boundaries between concepts."},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":55,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":56,"text":"### Cross-reference with code"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":57,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":58,"text":"When the user states how something works, check whether the code agrees. If you find a contradiction, surface it: \"Your code cancels entire Orders, but you just said partial cancellation is possible — which is right?\""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":59,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":60,"text":"### Update CONTEXT.md inline"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":61,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":62,"text":"When a term is resolved, update `CONTEXT.md` right there. Don't batch these up — capture them as they happen. Use the format in [CONTEXT-FORMAT.md](./CONTEXT-FORMAT.md)."},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":63,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":64,"text":"`CONTEXT.md` should be totally devoid of implementation details. Do not treat `CONTEXT.md` as a spec, a scratch pad, or a repository for implementation decisions. It is a glossary and nothing else."},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":65,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":66,"text":"### Offer ADRs sparingly"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":67,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":68,"text":"Only offer to create an ADR when all three are true:"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":69,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":70,"text":"1. **Hard to reverse** — the cost of changing your mind later is meaningful"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":71,"text":"2. **Surprising without context** — a future reader will wonder \"why did they do it this way?\""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":72,"text":"3. **The result of a real trade-off** — there were genuine alternatives and you picked one for specific reasons"},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":73,"text":""},{"sha":"aa7147f27ec7b9041c123246d38eea723f1c4e8c","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1781980281,"line":74,"text":"If any of the three is missing, skip the ADR. Use the format in [ADR-FORMAT.md](./ADR-FORMAT.md)."}]}
